(begin-tx "CONF-07 — IGNIS|C>DEBIT: the gas-balance floor")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [CONF-07 · 01 · gas debit floor] ---")
;;The companion to CONF-06g/h, which pin the TRANSFER amount rules. This one is the balance check:
;;an account cannot be debited more GAS than it holds. Without it the virtual-chain gas ledger
;;could go negative, which is the one thing a gas meter must never do.
;;
;;A REAL account is used with an absurd amount, rather than a dummy id with a small one. Both trip
;;the guard, but only the real account makes the failure attributable to the BALANCE — with a
;;dummy id the same message could equally mean "this account has no row at all".
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
(map print
    [
        (expect-failure "<<CONF-07>> debiting more GAS than the account holds is refused"
            "Insufficient GAS for GAS-Debiting"
            (test-capability (IGNIS.IGNIS|C>DEBIT KST.ANHD 999999999.0)))
    ]
)
(print "===^^^===")
(commit-tx)
(print "")
